     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pre-harvest tools are used for training (shape/framework of tree) and pruning of fruit trees, weeding, and disease control. Pre-harvest inputs include: IPM materials, ecofriendly/organic pesticides/bio-agents, botanical pesticides, blue and yellow sticky traps purpose control to reduce chemical hazards. Harvest horticulture inputs include saplings and grapevines cannot be counted under this indicator but can be counted under 1.3 below. No post-harvest or value addition tools or inputs are counted under this indicator; all processing related equipment falls under indicator 2.1, therefore the farmers receiving pre-harvest and harvest tools under Output 1 must be the same beneficiaries receiving post-harvest and processing tools/training under Output 2.</narrative>
